FatQat CUDA backend

This product is a fork of FatQat (https://github.com/spaceqat/fatqat),
developed by the FatQat contributors and licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0. The FatQat source, documentation and tests are their work.

This fork adds a CUDA engine for the FatQat simulator (statevector,
density-matrix, unitary and superoperator execution on NVIDIA GPUs through
CuPy, including per-shot trajectories), cache and shared-memory gate tiles
for the Numba and CUDA engines, exact circuit simplification, exact shot
branching, several GPUs for parameter sweeps and for a run's shots, an
Apple-GPU (Metal) runtime and its prototype, automatic runtime selection,
and their tests, benchmarks and documentation.
Those additions and modifications are Copyright 2026 CHOI Hei Wang (Oscar)
and are licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. They were developed
by a student at The Chinese University of Hong Kong, inspired by the course
CENG5280.

